Kubernetes HPA hands-on workflow

Step 1:Check Metrics Server
kubectl get pods -n kube-system              -- Look for metrics-server with Running status.
kubectl top pods
kubectl top nodes                             

Remember: A running Metrics Server Pod does not guarantee that metrics are available.

Step 2: Create the Deployment
kubectl apply -f my-app.yaml
kubectl get deployment my-app
kubectl get pods

resources:
  requests:
    cpu: "100m"
    memory: "128Mi"
  limits:
    cpu: "500m"
    memory: "257Mi"

Step 3: Expose your application
kubectl expose deployment my-app --port=80 --type=NodePort
kubectl get svc

Step 4: Create the HPA
Your hpa-app.yaml can target CPU or memory.
For CPU utilization:
metrics:
  - type: Resource
    resource:
      name: cpu
      target:
        type: Utilization
        averageUtilization: 70
For memory utilization, change name: cpu to name: memory.
kubectl apply -f hpa-app.yaml
kubectl get hpa
kubectl describe hpa hpa-app

Step 5: Generate load and watch scaling
Create a load-generator Pod:
kubectl run load-generator \
  --image=busybox:1.36 \
  --restart=Never \
  -- /bin/sh -c "while true; do wget -q -O- http://my-app; done"

Terminal 1:
kubectl get hpa hpa-app --watch
Terminal 2:
kubectl get deployment my-app -w
Terminal 3:
kubectl top pods

